# SE "device removed" is not the crash

Space Engineers always reports a render failure as DXGI `DEVICE_REMOVED` (`0x887A0005`) at `MyRender11.Present()`. A GPU hang, TDR, or driver reset looks identical in the log. Keen then sets `IsGPU: True` and prints Aftermath (`Get Info fail` is common). That Present failure is the **wrapper**, not the fault.

Do **not** treat "the device was removed" or "the GPU was unplugged" as the diagnosis. The driver already reset; SE has no other category for a dead device.

```text
# BAD
HRESULT 0x887A0005 DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED at Present — the GPU/device was lost.

# GOOD
Present failed after a GPU/driver reset. Find the hang or invalid work in the
frames before Present (Anomaly.debug.log, VRageRender-DirectX11_*.log, last
Anomaly/pack/DLSS lines). Device-removed is how SE reports that reset.
```

Look at work queued **before** `Exception in render!`: last compiled/drawn Anomaly pass, pack fullscreen, DLSS evaluate, RTV+SRV hazards, unbounded shader loops, Inf/NaN motion vectors. Aftermath missing does not mean "not a GPU crash."
